      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-6{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{36},\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-6{a}_{1}=-6(\\frac{1}{36})=-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-6{a}_{2}=-6(-\\frac{1}{6})=1 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-6{a}_{3}=-6(1)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{4}=-6.$",
